    "processes_each_tick": [
      "Six new flu patients arrive on average each day, with arrivals varying around that mean, and are admitted only when staffed beds are available.",
      "Each hospitalized patient occupies one bed until recovery or death.",
      "Patients requiring ventilation continue to require one ventilator until recovery, death, or a change in clinical status.",
      "Patients receiving ventilation have a 0.10 probability per day of recovering and leaving ventilation.",
      "Patients receiving ventilation have a 0.03 probability per day of dying.",
      "Patients requiring ventilation but not receiving it have a 0.15 probability per day of dying.",
      "Patients who recover leave the hospitalized population and free one bed and, if applicable, one ventilator.",
      "Patients who die leave the hospitalized population and free one bed and, if applicable, one ventilator.",
      "Each operational ventilator in use has a 0.005 probability per day of failing; a failed ventilator becomes unavailable and releases its patient to the unventilated waiting population.",
      "Ventilator orders advance through their delivery delay, and delivered ventilators increase hospital ventilator capacity and availability.",
      "Ventilator demand and waiting patients are updated after arrivals, clinical transitions, recoveries, deaths, and equipment failures."
